G1="Unity without truth"
G2="Unity without justice"
G3="Unity without mercy"
G4="Unity without sacrifice"
E=[
(G1,294,"**A unity without truth is a lie agreed upon.** Consider","**A unity without truth is a lie agreed upon.** A family can be fair, forgiving and devoted to one another and still refuse to face what is true. Consider"),
(G2,296,"**A unity without justice is a conspiracy of the strong.** Where some members are treated unfairly—denied the fair pay, honest dealing, respect or care that justice says is theirs—what looks like communion is really some people using others: the mother","**A unity without justice lives at someone else's expense.** A family can be honest, affectionate and quick to forgive, and still not give each member the respect, fairness, gratitude or care that justice says is theirs. Then the cost falls quietly on a few: the mother"),
(G2,296,"Such arrangements feel stable precisely because the cost is being silently absorbed by the powerless. But a body cannot be one while quietly devouring its own weaker members; the moment they can leave, they often do.","Such a home can feel warm and stable precisely because someone is silently absorbing the cost. But a body cannot stay one while some members carry what all should share; sooner or later they give out, or they leave."),
(G3,298,"**A unity without mercy cannot survive the first failure.** Every actual communion","**A unity without mercy cannot survive the first failure.** A family can be honest, fair and hardworking and still never forgive. Every actual communion"),
(G4,300,"**A unity without sacrifice is a fair-weather alliance.** It holds only as long as belonging costs nothing.","**A unity without sacrifice is a fair-weather alliance.** A family can be honest, fair and forgiving, and still give one another only what is convenient. Such a unity holds only as long as belonging costs nothing."),
]
